  "baseline_instrumentation_patch": "--- a/src/engine/audiofile/BufferedFileReader.h\n+++ b/src/engine/audiofile/BufferedFileReader.h\n@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@\n #include \"../../foundation/AutoResetEvent.h\"\n \n #include <atomic>\n+#include <cstddef>\n #include <cstdint>\n #include <memory>\n #include <thread>\n@@ -47,6 +48,14 @@\n     BufferedFileReader& operator= (const BufferedFileReader&) = delete;\n \n     const FileInfo& info() const noexcept { return fileInfo; }\n+    std::uint64_t workerWakeups() const noexcept\n+    {\n+        return workerWakeCount.load (std::memory_order_relaxed);\n+    }\n+    std::size_t windowAllocatedBytes() const noexcept\n+    {\n+        return ring.capacity() * sizeof (float) + fillDest.capacity() * sizeof (float*);\n+    }\n \n     // Audio thread. Copies the resident part of [startFrame, startFrame +\n     // numFrames) into dest, zero-filling the rest; destination channels past\n@@ -93,6 +102,7 @@\n     std::atomic<std::uint64_t> generation    { 0 };   // odd while the window is in flux\n \n     std::atomic<bool> stop { false };\n+    std::atomic<std::uint64_t> workerWakeCount { 0 };\n     AutoResetEvent    wake;\n     std::thread       worker;\n };\n--- a/src/engine/audiofile/BufferedFileReader.cpp\n+++ b/src/engine/audiofile/BufferedFileReader.cpp\n@@ -78,6 +78,7 @@\n         const bool moving = (h != lastHint);\n         lastHint = h;\n         wake.wait (moving ? kActiveWaitMs : kIdleWaitMs);\n+        workerWakeCount.fetch_add (1, std::memory_order_relaxed);\n     }\n }\n \n",
  "scope": "Standalone real BufferedFileReader and ReaderFillPool workload; warm page cache, paced 360 regions across 24 stereo tracks; no device or DSP. Runs were serial on an idle host. These results are separate from the full-engine DUSKSTUDIO_PERF_SESSION case.",
  "interpretation": [
    "New pool has no uncovered misses or wrong source frames in all three modes. Baseline locate has 52 uncovered read misses.",
    "Resident bytes are sampled; baseline includes an estimated 8192-frame FileReader scratch allocation per region. Process RSS includes the harness.",
    "Wait returns count worker timeout/notification returns, not OS scheduler wake-ups.",
    "Callback timings are single-run measurements; locate priming runs outside the callback."
  ],
